page('about.html','About Us','''<div class="page-intro" data-section="about-introduction"><h1>About Us</h1><p class="deck">Questions in the public interest. Reporting with a purpose.</p></div><div class="prose" data-section="mission"><h2>The Mission</h2><p>Civic Ledger is an invented nonprofit newsroom created for a website research study. Its stories explore how institutions make decisions and how those decisions reach people’s everyday lives.</p><p>We use original sample reporting to demonstrate a newsroom’s information architecture. No article describes real people or organizations.</p><section id="standards" data-section="editorial-standards"><h2>Our editorial approach</h2><p>In this demo, documents, context and clear explanations come first. Sources, writers and reported outcomes are fictional. A real newsroom would verify every claim before publication.</p></section><section id="local" data-section="local-reporting"><h2>Reporting together</h2><p>The local-reporting model brings subject knowledge and community questions into the same conversation. Our sample collaborations exist only as explanatory content.</p></section><section id="support" data-section="support-information"><h2>Support independent reporting</h2><p>This research replica does not accept donations. The source’s donation affordance is represented by this information section; there is no payment form or transaction.</p><a href="newsletters.html">Explore the newsletter simulation</a></section><section id="contact" data-section="contact-information"><h2>Contact and corrections</h2><p>This fictional organization has no monitored contact channel. For study feedback, contact your research facilitator. No personal information is collected by this site.</p></section></div><section class="band" data-section="about-latest"><h2>Latest Stories</h2><div class="two-grid">'''+card(0)+card(2)+'''</div></section>''')
